      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What size octopus rug should I buy?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Measure the clear floor span at its narrowest point and subtract about four inches at each edge. These rugs come on two ladders: square sizes of 24\"x24\", 36\"x36\", 48\"x48\", 60\"x60\" and 72\"x72\", and rectangular sizes of 24\"x36\", 36\"x60\", 48\"x72\" and 60\"x96\". If your measurement falls between two rungs, the smaller one almost always looks more deliberate."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is a round octopus rug better than a rectangular one?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on the floor, not on taste. Octopus artwork is radial, so round and square shapes let the tentacles reach outward evenly and the design reads from any approach. Rectangles impose a top and a bottom, which suits scene designs such as reefs, waves and compass roses more than a single centred creature."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the difference between a tentacle rug and a full octopus scene?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A tentacle design crops in close, so texture and suction cups fill the frame; it still reads as a complete image even when furniture covers half of it. A full scene places the octopus in an environment, which looks better on clear floors but loses its point when a table covers the centre."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much do octopus rugs cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Across the collection, prices run from $31.90 to $136.90, and the figure is driven by size rather than by design. The smallest sizes, 24\"x24\" and 24\"x36\", start at $31.90; 36\"x36\" starts at $53.90, 48\"x48\" at $63.90, 60\"x60\" at $93.90 and 72\"x72\" at $123.90."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Will an octopus carpet work on a warm wooden floor?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Often, but check the design first. Most octopus artwork runs cool, in teals and deep ocean blues, which can sit awkwardly on oak or terracotta. Designs with a warm accent running through them, or with metallic detail in the suction cups, bridge the gap; so do darker graphic designs that work on shape rather than colour harmony."
      }
    }
  ]
}
